WEBVTT

00:03.050 --> 00:06.880
To be honest, I don't understand 
how Satsuki could have failed.

00:08.650 --> 00:12.030
Go, Kitauji!

01:47.550 --> 01:48.690
Sensei...

01:49.140 --> 01:54.840
When you get older, just seeing young people 
working hard is enough to bring you to tears.

01:57.630 --> 01:59.830
Okay, here we go.

02:01.430 --> 02:03.420
<i>Second week of August.</i>

02:03.420 --> 02:06.090
<i>Team Monaka wins gold.</i>

02:06.100 --> 02:10.590
<b>Next, the competition members are going to win 
gold at the Kansai Competition no matter what!!</b>

02:06.420 --> 02:10.590
<i>Next, the competition members are going to win 
gold at the Kansai Competition no matter what.</i>

02:10.600 --> 02:12.110
<b>Congrats
 Concert Band
 Kansai Concert Band 
Competition Qualification</b>

02:10.600 --> 02:12.110
<b>Congrats
 Concert Band
 Kyoto Concert Band
 Competition Gold</b>

02:17.870 --> 02:23.420
<i>Tell Taki-sensei that, to that end, we need 
him to go full Spartan and whip us into shape.</i>

02:19.110 --> 02:23.370
<b>Tell Taki-sensei that, to that end, we need 
him to go full Spartan and whip us into shape.</b>

02:23.420 --> 02:24.620
<b>Even more Spartan?!</b>

02:23.420 --> 02:25.460
<i>Even more Spartan?!</i>

02:28.880 --> 02:34.070
If you have a staccato on Bars 5 and 6 of 
Rehearsal A, please emphasize it more.

02:34.070 --> 02:35.700
It sounds like it's dragging.

02:35.700 --> 02:36.460
Yes.

02:36.870 --> 02:41.250
If you have the theme, 
please be mindful of that phrase.

02:41.250 --> 02:41.600
Yes.

02:43.550 --> 02:47.060
I think my biggest question is: "How can we keep the members motivated?"

02:43.550 --> 02:47.600
<i>I think my biggest question is: "How can we keep the members motivated?"</i>

02:47.060 --> 02:49.450
She's talking like a real president!

02:47.600 --> 02:49.450
<i>She's talking like a real president!</i>

02:49.310 --> 02:51.430
You ought to learn from her.

02:49.450 --> 02:51.430
<i>You ought to learn from her.</i>

02:57.180 --> 03:03.410
<i>In all three summers of high school, all 
that awaited me was practice for days on end.</i>

03:03.980 --> 03:08.530
<i>The only </i>real<i> breaks we had, 
when we had no practice,</i>

03:08.530 --> 03:11.190
<i>were on the three days of the Bon Festival.</i>

03:12.670 --> 03:16.550
<b>Episode 7</b>

03:12.670 --> 03:16.550
<b>Summer Fermata</b>

03:16.550 --> 03:18.800
<b>Music Room</b>

03:17.970 --> 03:20.800
Those seeking to participate in the 
Kansai Concert Band Competition

03:18.800 --> 03:20.800
Kansai Concert Band Competition Preparation

03:20.800 --> 03:23.300
will be auditioning on 
the first day of camp.

03:23.300 --> 03:25.300
Competition members will 
be announced on the fifth.

03:25.590 --> 03:28.120
Soloists will be chosen then as well.

03:29.300 --> 03:33.330
The roster may change as a 
result of the auditions.

03:33.330 --> 03:37.680
But I like to believe that's because 
Kitauji itself is improving.

03:37.680 --> 03:43.360
What I'm trying to say is: Let's focus on 
winning the Kansai Competition for now.

03:43.360 --> 03:44.260
Yes.

03:48.140 --> 03:51.710
Why are the B team members called "Monaka"?

03:52.020 --> 03:54.000
Oh, because...

04:01.840 --> 04:02.960
Mayu-chan.

04:03.520 --> 04:04.170
Umm...

04:04.170 --> 04:07.660
Hey, President, I have a question.

04:08.270 --> 04:09.710
I'll see you up ahead.

04:10.340 --> 04:13.240
About the audition order...

04:13.240 --> 04:14.470
Oh, yeah.

04:20.450 --> 04:21.600
Okay, good.

04:21.600 --> 04:23.340
Next with a crescendo.

04:23.340 --> 04:24.450
Right.

04:24.450 --> 04:25.860
Here we go.

04:39.880 --> 04:43.220
Your tone is nasty, Kamaya-san.

04:43.220 --> 04:46.000
We're practicing playing as loud as we can.

04:46.000 --> 04:48.020
I think it's fine for now.

04:48.020 --> 04:51.580
Suzume's got so much dynamic range.

04:51.580 --> 04:54.060
Is that a compliment?

04:54.060 --> 04:57.480
You might sound really cool 
if you're playing jazz.

04:58.390 --> 05:02.250
Can we play some at our 
next performance, then?

05:02.250 --> 05:04.290
We still have the competition first.

05:04.290 --> 05:04.820
Right.

05:04.820 --> 05:08.030
Such a Keener McFirstYearer.

05:11.670 --> 05:13.220
I'm here.

05:13.220 --> 05:14.440
Sorry I'm—

05:14.440 --> 05:16.800
Huh, where's Mayu-chan?

05:16.800 --> 05:19.880
She said she's going to go 
play on her own for a bit.

05:20.790 --> 05:22.060
Oh.

05:23.620 --> 05:26.390
So hot.

05:26.390 --> 05:29.210
They said it's going to hit 36 today.

05:29.210 --> 05:32.340
How can you sit there so casually?

05:32.340 --> 05:36.150
You can just overcome hot and 
cold with willpower, right?

05:36.150 --> 05:37.630
You can, huh?

05:37.630 --> 05:40.060
Anyway, what are you doing on the Bon break?

05:40.060 --> 05:41.530
It's in two days.

05:41.530 --> 05:43.730
I haven't decided anything yet.

05:43.730 --> 05:47.010
You have trumpet classes, don't you?

05:47.540 --> 05:49.330
I do, I guess.

05:49.330 --> 05:51.040
But not all the time.

05:53.060 --> 05:54.380
What's your point?

05:54.790 --> 05:55.970
I mean...

05:57.120 --> 05:58.330
You mean?

05:58.710 --> 06:00.220
What's your problem?!

06:00.220 --> 06:01.930
No, that's not fair.

06:01.930 --> 06:06.350
I mean, we're going to have less 
time to hang out during break.

06:06.350 --> 06:08.850
Oh, that's what this is about.

06:08.850 --> 06:11.310
Sure, I'll miss you, too.

06:11.310 --> 06:12.550
That sounds so fake.

06:12.550 --> 06:12.890
<b>Train Arriving</b>

06:13.100 --> 06:15.700
<i>The train is now arriving.</i>

06:15.220 --> 06:18.020
The train's coming.

06:15.700 --> 06:18.020
<i>Please be careful.</i>

06:18.020 --> 06:19.340
Why don't you go ahead?

06:19.340 --> 06:22.790
Seriously, what's wrong? I don't get it.

06:22.790 --> 06:24.050
I mean, the p...

06:24.450 --> 06:25.230
P?

06:26.250 --> 06:30.180
Aren't we going to the pool this summer?

06:30.550 --> 06:31.630
The pool?

06:34.530 --> 06:35.490
Forget it.

06:36.700 --> 06:38.770
I'll go, I'll go.

06:38.770 --> 06:41.980
I just didn't think you'd have time 
with entrance exams and stuff.

06:41.980 --> 06:44.460
I told you, it's not going 
to be for the whole time.

06:44.460 --> 06:47.690
You can't expect me to figure 
you out from just <i>that</i>.

06:47.690 --> 06:49.540
I even bought a matching swimsuit, too.

06:50.510 --> 06:51.710
Fine.

06:51.710 --> 06:53.800
Why don't we call the others and...

06:55.130 --> 06:56.360
What?

06:56.360 --> 06:58.490
Do you mind if I invite Mayu-chan?

06:59.280 --> 07:01.330
I don't care.

07:02.460 --> 07:04.540
I'll ask a few more people, too.

07:03.360 --> 07:05.320
<b>College Information Sessions</b>

07:03.360 --> 07:05.320
It's summertime! Hit the pools!

07:03.360 --> 07:05.320
<b>Dream Park</b>

07:05.310 --> 07:06.450
The pool?

07:06.730 --> 07:07.640
Yeah.

07:07.640 --> 07:11.040
I'm going with Reina and some 
people from the bass section.

07:11.040 --> 07:12.490
You're welcome to join us.

07:12.920 --> 07:13.960
Let's go!

07:13.960 --> 07:15.550
Are you sure, though?

07:15.550 --> 07:17.710
Of course.

07:17.710 --> 07:18.890
I can't wait.

07:18.890 --> 07:20.920
Let's see, who else...

07:21.040 --> 07:22.920
Oumae, Kousaka, Kato, Kawashima,
 Kuroe, Kamaya T, Hisaishi, Suzuki S,
 Suzuki M, Kamaya S, Hariya, 
Kamiishi, Yoshii

07:21.280 --> 07:24.290
Ririka said she wanted to go, too.

07:24.290 --> 07:25.570
Really?

07:25.570 --> 07:30.010
Which means we'll have four
first-years and four second-years...

07:30.010 --> 07:31.600
That's a lot.

07:31.600 --> 07:35.510
I'll make a group chat 
just in case we need it.

07:35.510 --> 07:37.200
What about Motomu-kun?

07:37.200 --> 07:39.860
I dunno about inviting just one of the guys.

07:40.310 --> 07:43.880
Why don't you invite Tsukamoto-senpai, then?

07:46.350 --> 07:48.760
I think I'll pass on that.

07:48.760 --> 07:54.530
Though, Ririka and I are going to a 
college event on the first day of break.

07:54.530 --> 07:55.870
An event?

07:56.070 --> 08:05.540
<b>College Information Sessions</b>

07:56.720 --> 07:58.700
Oh, I've heard of this.

07:58.700 --> 08:02.120
It's where a bunch of colleges get 
together to give out information, right?

08:02.120 --> 08:06.120
Did you have plans to 
go, too, Kumiko-senpai?

08:06.120 --> 08:08.010
Not really.

08:08.010 --> 08:10.240
Wait, aren't you in second-year still?

08:10.240 --> 08:12.320
Isn't that normal?

08:16.310 --> 08:18.770
Maybe I should go.

08:18.760 --> 08:20.770
Information on many colleges,
 junior colleges and trade schools!

08:18.760 --> 08:20.770
<b>College Information Sessions</b>

08:18.760 --> 08:20.770
For: Exam students, high school students, parents and guardians, high school career planning teachers

08:18.760 --> 08:20.770
Free entry!

08:20.770 --> 08:22.390
Pre-Bon Break Concert Band Cleanup

08:20.770 --> 08:22.390
1:30 PM: Music Room, Instrument storage, Multi-use Classroom

08:20.770 --> 08:22.390
3:30 PM: Each section's classrooms, take out trash

08:20.770 --> 08:26.220
<i>And so our plans for our barely three-day 
summer break filled in instantly.</i>

08:27.010 --> 08:32.850
Everyone, why do we have this weird outfit?

08:33.610 --> 08:36.660
It's the Tuba-kun that 
Kumiko-chan was wearing!

08:36.660 --> 08:38.320
The president wore that?

08:38.320 --> 08:39.760
This takes me back.

08:39.760 --> 08:40.650
Right, Kumiko-chan?

08:40.650 --> 08:42.270
I guess.

08:42.270 --> 08:44.000
Huh?

08:44.530 --> 08:48.050
I told you we should have come another day.

08:48.050 --> 08:51.550
You were the one who said 
we only have today.

08:50.180 --> 08:51.550
Yuko-senpai.

08:51.550 --> 08:52.890
Natsuki-senpai!

08:52.890 --> 08:54.970
President Oumae.

08:54.970 --> 08:57.580
Looks like you have more members!

08:57.580 --> 08:58.840
You're so good at this.

08:58.840 --> 09:00.310
Oh, nah...

09:00.310 --> 09:02.130
This is so nostalgic, though.

09:02.130 --> 09:04.360
I'd forgotten this smell.

09:04.360 --> 09:07.380
Not that I ever noticed when I was here.

09:09.940 --> 09:11.390
It's so dusty!

09:10.730 --> 09:12.290
They're in the middle of cleaning.

09:12.290 --> 09:13.240
Of course it is.

09:14.680 --> 09:15.730
Your hairpins...

09:16.660 --> 09:19.630
She's just ripping me off.

09:19.630 --> 09:20.760
What?

09:20.760 --> 09:23.170
I was the one who bought it first.

09:23.170 --> 09:25.050
Do you really want to copy me that badly?

09:25.650 --> 09:28.060
You idiot, you idiot, you idiot!

09:28.060 --> 09:29.590
Whoa, single breath.

09:29.590 --> 09:30.880
Shut up!

09:30.880 --> 09:33.390
Would you mind chilling out a little?

09:33.890 --> 09:35.970
You've creeped out the first-years.

09:35.970 --> 09:38.910
I-I'm Hariya Kaho, in first-year.

09:38.910 --> 09:41.510
I-I have the pleasure of playing euphonium.

09:41.510 --> 09:44.220
Euph, huh?

09:46.440 --> 09:49.220
She's already better than 
you, Natsuki-senpai.

09:50.290 --> 09:52.240
I'm glad to hear it.

09:56.030 --> 09:57.700
It looks so good!

09:57.700 --> 09:59.290
First come, first served, right?

09:59.290 --> 10:00.160
I'm taking this one.

10:00.160 --> 10:01.610
I want vanilla.

10:01.610 --> 10:03.780
Kanade-chan, which one would you like?

10:03.780 --> 10:06.490
I'm on a diet, so I'll pass.

10:06.490 --> 10:09.060
Really? I'll take two, then.

10:09.060 --> 10:12.160
You shouldn't. You'll get sick.

10:12.810 --> 10:15.930
So, how goes drum majoring?

10:15.930 --> 10:18.390
I'm reasonably satisfied with myself.

10:18.390 --> 10:21.600
Must be going well then, if you say so.

10:21.600 --> 10:24.460
I think we made the right choice, 
having you three be the execs.

10:24.460 --> 10:25.470
Yeah.

10:25.470 --> 10:28.010
So, how's Kansai?

10:28.010 --> 10:28.810
Can you make it?

10:29.070 --> 10:32.740
Ryusei, Myoujou and Toushou 
are all there again, right?

10:32.740 --> 10:33.540
Yes.

10:33.540 --> 10:36.940
But the advisory teacher 
moved to another school,

10:36.940 --> 10:39.650
so I don't think they're as 
good as they were before.

10:39.650 --> 10:42.510
And now that teacher's in Ryusei, right?

10:42.510 --> 10:46.690
You'll have to be able to go up against 
them to make it to the Nationals, huh?

10:46.690 --> 10:47.950
Probably.

10:48.450 --> 10:51.840
Well, we'll come cheer you on if 
you make it to the Nationals.

10:51.840 --> 10:54.960
Not that I know if we'll win the lottery.

10:55.250 --> 10:59.060
I think everyone would be 
happy to know you're coming.

10:59.060 --> 11:01.850
Kousaka? Flattering people? 
Didn't see that coming.

11:01.850 --> 11:03.480
No, I mean it.

11:03.480 --> 11:04.980
She's a third-year.

11:04.980 --> 11:06.870
Everyone's grown up.

11:06.870 --> 11:08.260
Unlike you.

11:08.260 --> 11:10.960
I'm grown up, too!

11:20.210 --> 11:23.820
<i>And so begins our brief summer break.</i>

11:24.830 --> 11:26.450
<b>College Information Sessions</b>

11:29.170 --> 11:31.920
Man, there's so many people.

11:31.920 --> 11:33.540
Is there anything you're 
interested in in particular?

11:33.540 --> 11:34.780
Nope.

11:34.780 --> 11:36.790
I should have brought Midori along.

11:37.180 --> 11:39.130
"That place is known for whatever thing!"

11:39.130 --> 11:41.330
I can see her saying.

11:41.330 --> 11:44.640
Midori-chan already knows which 
college she's aiming for.

11:44.640 --> 11:49.180
Why don't we take a lap around and 
then visit the interesting ones?

11:49.180 --> 11:49.760
Okay.

11:51.350 --> 11:52.190
<b>Fly to the World</b>

11:53.980 --> 11:54.980
<b>Kyoto International University</b>

11:53.980 --> 11:54.980
A fulfilling 
place to learn
 Build Your Future

12:05.320 --> 12:07.490
<b>Prepare to do
 what you want!</b>

12:11.060 --> 12:12.160
Yikes.

12:12.500 --> 12:15.100
The emotional damage is just...

12:15.100 --> 12:16.120
Yikes.

12:16.120 --> 12:18.500
It was so crowded, too.

12:18.500 --> 12:21.250
Like, what birthrate decline?

12:21.250 --> 12:24.020
Though, I think I kinda have some ideas now.

12:25.180 --> 12:29.160
Everyone at the venue is trying 
to get to college, right?

12:29.160 --> 12:31.400
That means we have to be ready.

12:31.400 --> 12:32.240
Uh-huh.

12:32.570 --> 12:33.480
Okay.

12:33.880 --> 12:36.240
I'm going to junior college.

12:36.240 --> 12:38.140
Somewhere I can get a 
nursery-school teacher license.

12:38.470 --> 12:40.110
Huh? What? Huh?

12:40.110 --> 12:42.700
Hazuki-chan, you want to become 
a nursery school teacher?!

12:42.700 --> 12:44.860
It's only recently that I had the thought.

12:44.860 --> 12:51.540
Michie-sensei suggested it, saying 
I'm attentive and good with kids.

12:48.370 --> 12:52.870
<b>Department of Early Childhood Education
 Department of Nursery</b>

12:51.540 --> 12:52.860
That's all it took?!

12:52.860 --> 12:55.530
Not just that, but...

12:55.530 --> 13:00.620
She asked if I was interested, 
which made me think, maybe I am.

13:01.930 --> 13:03.090
Yeah?

13:04.500 --> 13:10.120
You wouldn't know it, but Michie-sensei 
really pays attention to each one of us.

13:10.120 --> 13:11.350
Isn't she awesome?

13:11.350 --> 13:12.390
True.

13:12.390 --> 13:17.110
She remembers everyone's 
personalities and aspirations.

13:17.110 --> 13:17.850
Yeah.

13:21.360 --> 13:23.650
Teachers are amazing.

13:25.990 --> 13:29.580
It might be kinda fun if 
you're a teacher, Kumiko.

13:30.300 --> 13:35.710
You get a job at a high school, and you 
show up in a suit, and you're, like...

13:36.290 --> 13:38.070
"What is this?"

13:38.370 --> 13:40.050
Why am I Taki-sensei?

13:40.050 --> 13:41.600
I dunno, just cuz.

13:42.430 --> 13:44.830
Okay, I'll keep these two.

13:44.830 --> 13:46.720
Wanna look?

13:45.800 --> 13:47.550
<b>The Path to 
Post-Secondary</b>

13:45.800 --> 13:47.550
Joint Career 
Information Session

13:47.960 --> 13:51.400
<i>I didn't know how she could decide so quickly.</i>

13:51.400 --> 13:53.850
<i>Was I just weird?</i>

13:54.830 --> 14:01.210
<i>But there was no way I'd just wake up one 
day and know what I wanted to become.</i>

14:01.730 --> 14:07.780
<i>I couldn't bring myself 
to just decide on a whim, either.</i>

14:08.810 --> 14:10.620
I'm home.

14:11.530 --> 14:13.710
Welcome home.

14:14.210 --> 14:15.430
Nee-chan.

14:21.850 --> 14:23.410
How long are you staying?

14:23.410 --> 14:26.390
Probably just for the Bon season.

14:26.390 --> 14:29.370
So, how did the event go?

14:29.370 --> 14:30.360
The event?

14:30.360 --> 14:31.930
Yeah. For college.

14:31.930 --> 14:34.760
She still hasn't decided where she's going.

14:34.760 --> 14:35.720
Still?

14:35.720 --> 14:37.140
Summer break's almost over.

14:37.140 --> 14:38.800
I know that.

14:38.800 --> 14:40.430
I'm home.

14:40.810 --> 14:42.330
Welcome home.

14:42.780 --> 14:44.950
Mamiko. You're home.

14:44.950 --> 14:45.910
Yup.

14:46.760 --> 14:48.450
Here, a gift.

14:50.460 --> 14:51.820
Bath salts.

14:52.660 --> 14:56.980
It's normal not to know what you 
want to spend your life doing.

14:56.980 --> 14:58.860
You've been alive for 18 years.

14:58.860 --> 15:01.410
If you were going to find something, 
you already would have.

15:01.410 --> 15:03.790
Stop saying the same things as my friends.

15:04.150 --> 15:06.650
In any case, it's fine if you 
can't think of anything.

15:06.650 --> 15:08.580
Just find a stable job...

15:07.720 --> 15:10.120
I heard that a bajillion times already!

15:10.470 --> 15:14.150
Personally, I think you 
should do what you want.

15:14.990 --> 15:17.350
Yeah, that's part of the problem.

15:17.350 --> 15:21.360
If I quit college saying I want 
to become a beautician, too,

15:21.360 --> 15:23.680
Dad's going to lose faith in his parenting.

15:23.680 --> 15:24.610
Sorry.

15:24.610 --> 15:26.270
I really do feel bad about that.

15:26.580 --> 15:27.920
Think about what you've done!

15:27.920 --> 15:29.180
I am.

15:31.690 --> 15:34.530
That's what I mean, though.

15:34.530 --> 15:36.430
I had a hard time deciding, too.

15:36.430 --> 15:38.390
Embrace the struggle, my sister.

15:38.390 --> 15:39.840
What the hell?

15:39.840 --> 15:41.210
Mamiko.

15:41.580 --> 15:43.200
That was a nice bath.

15:44.240 --> 15:45.420
Right?

15:51.610 --> 15:54.250
I'm going in first.

15:54.250 --> 15:57.160
Senpai, no running!

15:57.160 --> 15:58.590
You're running, too, Sacchan.

15:58.590 --> 16:01.120
Our senpais all have such nice figures.

16:01.120 --> 16:02.390
We're still growing!

16:02.390 --> 16:05.350
We just need a year! It's fine!

16:05.350 --> 16:06.840
You can't be serious, right?

16:06.840 --> 16:09.110
You didn't need to say it out loud.

16:11.100 --> 16:14.330
Look what happens after one more year!

16:15.360 --> 16:17.970
Kousaka-senpai's in a different league.

16:17.970 --> 16:20.340
Hey, where's Hazuki-chan?

16:20.340 --> 16:22.070
She went ahead.

16:22.070 --> 16:23.350
Ah, okay.

16:23.350 --> 16:26.700
You both look so good.

16:26.700 --> 16:28.530
Thanks.

16:28.530 --> 16:31.400
It's kind of reassuring 
when you're both here.

16:31.400 --> 16:34.500
I hope you're still at Kitauji next year.

16:34.500 --> 16:36.560
I don't plan on flunking.

16:36.560 --> 16:40.110
Okay, we'll take turns watching 
our stuff. You guys can go ahead.

16:40.110 --> 16:41.170
Really?

16:41.170 --> 16:41.690
Yeah.

16:41.690 --> 16:43.530
See you!

16:46.390 --> 16:48.640
What about us?

16:51.400 --> 16:54.180
Okay, I'll be back.

16:54.180 --> 16:54.530
Sure.

16:58.290 --> 17:00.590
Where'd Tsubame-chan go?

17:00.590 --> 17:01.910
Oh, yeah.

17:02.340 --> 17:04.590
She just went to buy drinks.

17:04.590 --> 17:06.260
Got it.

17:06.260 --> 17:07.520
What about Kousaka-san?

17:07.520 --> 17:09.150
Same.

17:13.390 --> 17:15.260
It's hot, huh?

17:15.260 --> 17:16.180
It is.

17:16.180 --> 17:18.620
I'm glad the weather's nice, though.

17:21.160 --> 17:22.970
You have matching swimsuits, right?

17:22.970 --> 17:24.560
And you swapped tops and bottoms.

17:24.560 --> 17:26.070
You're so close. I love that.

17:26.070 --> 17:29.370
You're close with Tsubame-chan, 
too, aren't you?

17:29.370 --> 17:30.930
That's why you're our president.

17:30.930 --> 17:32.820
You know everything.

17:32.820 --> 17:33.890
Nah.

17:33.890 --> 17:35.390
I see you in class, too.

17:35.390 --> 17:37.460
And Suzume-chan's around, too.

17:37.460 --> 17:39.170
Yeah, I guess.

17:39.170 --> 17:41.620
Suzume-chan's so full of energy.

17:41.950 --> 17:45.390
She can talk to anyone and 
make friends with everyone.

17:45.390 --> 17:47.590
You're like that, too, aren't you?

17:48.390 --> 17:50.100
Not at all.

17:50.950 --> 17:53.260
How are you, then?

17:55.020 --> 17:56.250
I wonder.

17:56.820 --> 18:01.270
All our underclassmen say 
they love you, Mayu-chan.

18:01.620 --> 18:06.260
You're approachable and kind, 
and you teach them properly.

18:06.520 --> 18:09.970
That's because that's the best 
way to make everyone happy.

18:10.800 --> 18:13.160
So you'd rather not?

18:14.260 --> 18:15.660
I'm not sure.

18:18.420 --> 18:23.570
See, I think I have less of a 
sense of self than most people.

18:23.570 --> 18:26.400
I don't have many preferences, either.

18:26.400 --> 18:29.510
I'm fine with anything.

18:30.390 --> 18:36.590
<i>Those words gave me an idea of where 
my vague discomfort was coming from.</i>

18:38.090 --> 18:39.320
<i>This girl...</i>

18:40.320 --> 18:41.820
<i>Kuroe Mayu...</i>

18:42.910 --> 18:47.370
<i>Reminds me of myself in middle school.</i>

18:49.750 --> 18:53.890
Kitauji played <i>Liz and the 
Blue Bird</i> last year, right?

18:53.890 --> 18:55.690
Eh? Yeah.

18:56.470 --> 19:00.740
I can't help but think 
Liz is really selfish.

19:00.740 --> 19:03.900
She had plenty of animals 
that she spent time with.

19:03.900 --> 19:07.200
Why was she so fixated on the blue bird?

19:07.200 --> 19:08.080
True.

19:08.790 --> 19:13.580
Though, that's probably not 
the way most people see it.

19:14.650 --> 19:18.590
Most people fixate on one thing or another.

19:19.120 --> 19:21.160
You're that way, too, aren't you?

19:21.160 --> 19:25.270
You like this person. You hate that thing.

19:25.270 --> 19:30.300
I think it's a bit extreme to say you aren't 
normal if you aren't like that, though.

19:32.130 --> 19:33.650
You're right.

19:33.650 --> 19:35.860
But I still think...

19:36.870 --> 19:43.040
No one would ever love someone 
who isn't like that.

19:44.380 --> 19:47.260
I mean, I'm that way.

19:53.370 --> 19:54.660
I'm back.

19:56.360 --> 19:57.640
Hey.

19:57.640 --> 20:00.490
We saw Kamaya-san and decided 
to get some for everyone.

20:00.490 --> 20:03.440
We didn't know what people 
like, so we bought some extra.

20:03.440 --> 20:05.140
Ooh, thanks.

20:05.750 --> 20:07.870
Mayu-chan, which one do you want?

20:11.040 --> 20:13.230
What do you like, Tsubame-chan?

20:16.980 --> 20:19.250
Okay, look over here.

20:19.250 --> 20:20.570
Smile!

20:25.380 --> 20:28.800
I like your camera. It's so moody.

20:28.800 --> 20:30.530
My dad gave it to me.

20:31.240 --> 20:33.370
I like the color more than digital.

20:34.370 --> 20:37.050
Do you have any pictures from Seira?

20:37.360 --> 20:38.570
Of course.

20:38.570 --> 20:40.660
I have tons at home.

20:43.670 --> 20:46.630
<i>She gets along with everyone.</i>

20:46.630 --> 20:48.760
<i>No one hates her.</i>

20:50.630 --> 20:51.600
<i>But...</i>

20:52.100 --> 20:53.810
<i>Isn't that kinda...</i>

20:58.470 --> 20:59.820
Mayu-chan.

21:05.240 --> 21:09.170
I don't like being in pictures, though.

21:09.170 --> 21:10.950
We don't get to come all the time.

21:10.950 --> 21:13.640
I want at least one photo with you.

21:13.640 --> 21:14.540
Really?

21:14.540 --> 21:15.690
Look forward.

21:18.940 --> 21:25.850
<i>And so our brief summer break ended, and we 
were back to our life of endless practice.</i>

21:26.860 --> 21:28.470
Did you tan a bit, Reina?

21:30.050 --> 21:31.760
Ooh, sexy.

21:31.760 --> 21:33.370
So did you.

21:33.370 --> 21:37.010
My skin just turns red and goes right back.

21:38.660 --> 21:40.070
Good morning.

21:40.070 --> 21:41.650
Yume-chan. You're here early.

21:41.650 --> 21:42.630
Yes.

21:42.630 --> 21:44.490
I had some spare time.

21:44.490 --> 21:46.340
Plus, auditions are coming up.

21:46.340 --> 21:48.320
You'll be fine.

21:48.320 --> 21:49.820
That's not...

21:49.820 --> 21:54.290
No, Kabe-chan-senpai said 
no negative comments.

21:54.950 --> 21:56.250
Morning.

21:56.250 --> 21:57.560
Good morning.

21:57.560 --> 21:58.540
Morning.

21:58.540 --> 22:00.010
You're here early, too.

22:00.010 --> 22:00.680
Yeah.

22:00.680 --> 22:05.340
The photos are done, so I thought 
I'd show them off before practice.

22:07.980 --> 22:10.010
Holy crap, Kaho's funny face.

22:10.010 --> 22:11.660
So cute!

22:12.020 --> 22:14.030
It's weirdly charming.

22:14.330 --> 22:18.910
It could be even more expressive 
if I could change the lens.

22:19.450 --> 22:20.190
Huh?

22:20.530 --> 22:24.150
Hey, Mama-chan, where's that last 
picture you took with all of us?

22:24.660 --> 22:26.150
Oh, that one?

22:26.150 --> 22:28.310
It didn't develop properly.

22:28.730 --> 22:29.930
Sorry.

22:30.600 --> 22:32.070
Really?

22:32.600 --> 22:33.450
Yeah.

22:38.160 --> 22:39.510
Kumiko-chan...

22:40.630 --> 22:44.650
Why did you invite me? I wonder.

22:46.150 --> 22:51.220
I've been wondering if there's something 
you wanted to talk to me about.

22:51.960 --> 22:53.240
Mayu-chan...

22:53.240 --> 22:54.180
Hey...

22:54.680 --> 22:57.680
I'll play properly at the 
audition. Don't worry.

22:59.780 --> 23:04.120
You want the best people to 
be chosen at the auditions

23:04.120 --> 23:08.450
and for Kitauji to put on the best 
performance and win the gold, right?

23:09.100 --> 23:11.050
I get that.

23:18.040 --> 23:22.790
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:21.960 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
